<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000009> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000009> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000006> .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000009> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#disjointWith> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000028> .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000009> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000179> "2d-s-region" .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000009> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000180> "TwoDimensionalSpatialRegion" .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000009> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112> "an infinitely thin plane in space."@en .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000009> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112> "the surface of a sphere-shaped part of space"@en .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000009> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000600> "A two-dimensional spatial region is a spatial region that is of two dimensions. (axiom label in BFO2 Reference: [039-001])"@en .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000009> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000602> "(forall (x) (if (TwoDimensionalSpatialRegion x) (SpatialRegion x))) // axiom label in BFO2 CLIF: [039-001] " .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000009> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo.owl> .
