<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000142> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112> "The Equator"@en .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000142> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112> "all geopolitical boundaries"@en .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000142> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112> "all lines of latitude and longitude"@en .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000142> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112> "the line separating the outer surface of the mucosa of the lower lip from the outer surface of the skin of the chin."@en .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000142> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112> "the median sulcus of your tongue"@en .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000142> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000600> "a one-dimensional continuant fiat boundary is a continuous fiat line whose location is defined in relation to some material entity. (axiom label in BFO2 Reference: [032-001])"@en .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000142> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000602> "(iff (OneDimensionalContinuantFiatBoundary a) (and (ContinuantFiatBoundary a) (exists (b) (and (OneDimensionalSpatialRegion b) (forall (t) (locatedInAt a b t)))))) // axiom label in BFO2 CLIF: [032-001] " .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000142> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo.owl> .
